{"diagnosis": "Trace shows TRAP: no progress max_addr=0x00000000 with tohost FAIL 0xdead, i.e. zero fetches vs expected NOP-stream progress. Root cause in excerpt is the memory FSM idle state: picorv32.v:568 resets mem_state <= 1 and picorv32.v:582 labels the idle branch 1: begin, creating a duplicate 1: with picorv32.v:595 and leaving no 0 idle state. The FSM self-loops in the request branch and never reaches the mem_xfer wait handling, so mem_valid/mem fetch never progresses.",
 "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -565,7 +565,7 @@
 	always @(posedge clk) begin
 		if (!resetn || trap) begin
 			if (!resetn)
-				mem_state <= 1;
+				mem_state <= 0;
 			if (!resetn || mem_ready)
 				mem_valid <= 0;
 			mem_la_secondword <= 0;
@@ -579,8 +579,8 @@
 			end
 			case (mem_state)
-				1: begin
+				0: begin
 					if (mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst || mem_do_rdata) begin
 						mem_valid <= !mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word;
 						mem_instr <= mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst;
",
 "expected": "tohost PASS (not FAIL 0xdead) with max_addr progress >0x00000000 and no TRAP: no progress"}

